On Wed, Dec 17, 2003 at 01:28:21PM +0800, Yu, Luming wrote:
> >It's been a while since I've kept up with the acpi-development, but as
> >far as I remember, there were some problems switching between the
> >flatpanel and an external monitor on some ASUS centrino laptops (more
> >specifically the M2400N)

> Is this ACPI issue? If yes, please provide some detail.

Not as far as I know. The video driver is responsible for anything
more involved than what currently works. In particular, we'd need
driver support to drive both outputs independantly. The DSDT just
provides for cycling between LCD, CRT and LCD+CRT (cloned). The issue
that these combinations can only be cycled through, not set directly,
is due to the BIOS/DSDT, but not a big issue anyhow.

